This extension provides language support for DaeDaLus specifications.

The extension relies on a language server, which needs to be installed
separately (see below).


Packaging and Installing the VSCode Client
==========================================

The source code for the client is in this directory.
You'll need `node` already installed.

Install dependencies:

    npm install

Build a VSCode package:

    npm run package

If everything went OK you should see a file called `daedalus-`X.Y.Z`.vsix`.

To install the extension in VSCode, open the extensions tab, and from
the menu (three little dots) select "Install from VSIX".  Once the extension
is installed, open the settings, and find its settings to specify the
path to the language server binary.


Installing the Language Server
==============================

Build and install with:

    cabal install daedalus-language-server

Make sure the resulting `daedalus-language-server` executable is on your
`$PATH`, or point the `daedalus.language-server-path` VSCode setting at it.


Test
----

Open a DaeDaLus specification (a `.ddl` file).  VSCode should recognize
the file as `Daedalus` (in the bottom status bar).  You should get syntax
highlighting for the file, and when you hover over expressions you should
be able to see their type.
